      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2oy",
          "text": "What Is Dating App Liability?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2p5",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l2p2",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/sb24-011"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2p0",
          "text": "Dating app liability ",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2p1",
          "text": "in Colorado refers to the legal responsibility of online dating platforms when users suffer harm at the hands of other users. In response to high-profile incidents, Colorado enacted ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2p3",
          "text": "Senate Bill 24-011",
          "marks": [
            "strong",
            "l2p2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2p4",
          "text": ", which requires online dating services to adopt written safety policies for investigating reports of dangerous conduct.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2p7",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2p6",
          "text": "Consequently, lawsuits against platforms such as Hinge and Tinder seek to hold companies accountable when they receive credible reports of predatory behavior but fail to act. The legal focus centers on whether corporate inaction contributed to foreseeable harm. At the core, courts ask whether the platform exercised reasonable care once it received credible reports. Because a dating app controls profile creation and reporting systems, exposure to civil claims increases when it fails to respond to repeated complaints.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2p9",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2p8",
          "text": "Under Colorado law, a service operating without a compliant safety policy engages in a deceptive trade practice. This framework reflects a shift toward accountability beyond broad marketing promises.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "image",
      "_key": "i2pa",
      "src": "./images/2026-03-dating-app-liability.jpg",
      "alt": "dating app liability"
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2pc",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2pb",
          "text": "Are Dating Apps Responsible for User Safety?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2pe",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2pd",
          "text": "Dating apps may face responsibility when their own conduct contributes to foreseeable harm. Criminal acts remain the responsibility of the perpetrator, yet legal analysis does not end there. Courts examine whether the dating app received clear warnings about violent behavior, failed to suspend accounts after credible complaints, or represented safety measures that were never meaningfully enforced.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2pg",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2pf",
          "text": "When a platform prioritizes user growth over safety, legal scrutiny follows to determine whether corporate decisions increased foreseeable risk. Beyond these internal choices, once multiple reports flag an account for violent behavior, reliance on standard user agreements may no longer shield a platform from scrutiny. Ultimately, internal moderation systems and compliance with safety policies are the factors that influence whether harm could have been reduced in the eyes of the court.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2pi",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2ph",
          "text": "Colorado courts increasingly analyze these claims alongside federal immunity defenses, creating a developing legal landscape around online dating platform accountability.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2pk",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2pj",
          "text": "When Can a Dating App Be Held Liable for User Injuries?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2pm",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2pl",
          "text": "Liability turns on corporate conduct, not merely on the existence of a tragic event. In the evolving 2026 legal landscape, Colorado civil claims frequently center on whether the platform had notice of dangerous behavior and failed to act. We specifically examine whether aspects of the app’s design make it easier for dangerous users to operate or harder for victims to report misconduct. Common fact patterns include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2po",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2pn",
          "text": "Prior reports of assault or stalking tied to the same account.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2pq",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2pp",
          "text": "Failure to remove a user after credible, documented complaints.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2ps",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2pr",
          "text": "Design flaws that allow banned users to return via new profiles.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2pu",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s2pt",
          "text": "Advertising-enhanced screening that lacks actual verification.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b2q1",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l2px",
